<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muzaffar Shah I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1411">1411</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muzaffar Shah I, born Zafar Khan, was the founder of the Gujarat Sultanate. Appointed governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> by the Tughluq sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1391, he declared independence after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s sack of Delhi had left the sultanate powerless, taking the title of sultan around 1407. He was succeeded by his grandson Ahmad Shah I, who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmedabad">Ahmedabad</a> in 1411.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muzaffar-shah-i.jpg" alt="Muzaffar Shah I" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drnsreedhar1959 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:002Muzaffir-1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On 3 August 1347 one of their leaders, <b>Zafar Khan</b>, also known as Hasan Gangu, was proclaimed sultan as Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Zafar Khan</b>, governor of Gujarat for the Tughluqs, declared independence in 1407 as Muzaffar Shah after Timur's sack of Delhi left the Delhi Sultanate powerless.</blockquote><a href="/state/gujarat-sultanate">Gujarat Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>He was installed around 1528 as Sultan <b>Muzaffar Shah I</b>, founding a dynasty that still reigns.</blockquote><a href="/state/perak-sultanate">Perak Sultanate</a></li></ul></section>
